---
title: Prerelease publication · where the release set is checked
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Planned
  Planned --> LinuxBuilt : CI green; Linux jobs pass
  LinuxBuilt --> NativeBuilt : native bundle built
  NativeBuilt --> packageCheck : package
  state packageCheck <<choice>>
  packageCheck --> Packaged : [set matches metadata]
  packageCheck --> Refused : [mismatch]
  Packaged --> Approved : approval; CI, head rechecked
  Packaged --> Refused : upgrade gate fails
  Packaged --> [*] : prepare only
  Approved --> Refused : publish gate fails
  Approved --> publishCheck : verify assets
  state publishCheck <<choice>>
  publishCheck --> Tagged : [set matches metadata]
  publishCheck --> Refused : [mismatch]
  Tagged --> Published : twelve assets uploaded
  Tagged --> Refused : upload failed (tag kept)
  Published --> [*]
  Refused --> [*]
  note right of Packaged
    INV a packaged set lists exactly
    the platforms whose files it holds.
  end note
  note right of Tagged
    INV publish creates no tag for a set whose
    platform list differs from its files.
  end note
  class Planned idle
  class LinuxBuilt,NativeBuilt,Packaged live
  class Approved wait
  class Tagged,Published ok
  class Refused fail
